  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment history includes positive values (e.g., >0.00), as models tend to overreact to sentiment signals.",
    "Reduce forecast volatility in early periods (e.g., first 5-7 days) when price is trending upward — models often overshoot.",
    "Apply mean reversion correction: if forecast is >10% above recent 5-day average, reduce by 5-10%.",
    "For spikes in true outcome, lag correction: if forecast peaks 2-3 days before true peak, reduce by 5-10% to avoid overestimating momentum.",
    "When sentiment history is neutral (all 0.00), use historical 15-day moving average as baseline, but adjust downward 2-3% if true outcome is consistently higher than forecast.",
    "In late periods (e.g., last 10 days of forecast), increase downward bias if true outcome shows downward drift — models tend to overcorrect upward."
  ]
}
